sequenceDiagram
 participant A0 as Traveler UI
 participant A1 as Express services
 participant A2 as Sources and AI
 participant A3 as PostgreSQL
 A0->>A1: 1. Submit confirmed brief and idempotency key
 A1->>A3: 2. Begin/replay owner and request-hash record
 A1->>A2: 3. Load permitted venues; request bounded ID schedule
 A2->>A1: 4. Return references or labeled provider failure
 A1->>A3: 5. Store terminal generation result with attempt fencing
 A1->>A0: 6. Return validated schedule, costs and notices
 A0->>A1: 7. Explicit autosave with save identity and grounding
 A1->>A3: 8. Transaction: Trip, version and audit
 A1->>A0: 9. Saved identity or failure with recoverable local draft
